# Stage4 BASE package list — Orange Pi Zero 2 (Allwinner H616, arm64) HEADLESS
# APPLIANCE. One atom per line; lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# This is the ONLY package list this platform ever emerges from besides
# packages-live.list (bootable-flavor-only) — UNLIKE every desktop platform in
# this repo, there is NO packages-desktop.list / packages-light-desktop.list
# sibling: this board has no desktop mode, ever (see build-orangepi-zero2-stage4.sh's
# header + specs-orangepi-zero2/README.md for the HDMI/mainline-driver research
# that justifies this). What you see here IS the whole appliance.
#
# NOTE on the H616 boot chain (EXPERIMENTAL — see specs-orangepi-zero2/README.md):
#   * Boots via mainline U-Boot (orangepi_zero2_defconfig) with a GENUINELY
#     NATIVE (non-blob) DRAM-init driver — U-Boot's own drivers/ram/sunxi H616
#     DDR3 training code, no closed "boot0" blob at all. This is a real point of
#     difference from EVERY OTHER arm64 platform in this repo (Frite/Orange-Pi-5
#     both need at least one proprietary boot blob) — see the README.
#   * distro-boot then scans the first partition for /extlinux/extlinux.conf,
#     same mechanism as Frite/Orange-Pi-5. There is NO raspberrypi-firmware
#     blob and NO config.txt.
#   * The board-specific DTB ships from the KERNEL build (gentoo-sources /
#     mainline), NOT from a vendor firmware package.

# ── Kernel sources (mainline; the H616 device tree is upstream) ────────────
sys-kernel/gentoo-sources
sys-kernel/linux-firmware

# ── Bootloader tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# u-boot-tools provides mkimage (FIT/extlinux) used to assemble the boot blob;
# the actual U-Boot binary for the board is built/fetched by the builder (see
# --uboot-url — OPTIONAL here, unlike Frite/Orange-Pi-5: this board's mainline
# U-Boot needs NO proprietary blob at all, so a real from-source build is a
# realistic option a future contributor can wire up; --uboot-url still exists
# as the same override escape hatch every other platform has).
dev-embedded/u-boot-tools

# ── Board hardware / storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────
sys-block/parted
sys-apps/usbutils
sys-apps/util-linux
sys-fs/e2fsprogs
sys-fs/dosfstools

# ── Networking ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
net-misc/networkmanager
net-misc/openssh
net-firewall/iptables
net-misc/socat
# Egress VPN (split-tunnel, fail-closed) — wg-quick (WireGuard, first-class) +
# openvpn (fallback) for the node-level hugmesh-egress-vpn OpenRC service
# (DEFAULT-OFF; same plumbing as every other client image).
net-vpn/wireguard-tools
net-vpn/openvpn
# WiFi supplicant is present ONLY for a hypothetical USB WiFi dongle with its
# OWN mainline driver — the ONBOARD Unisoc UWE5622/AW859A radio has NO mainline
# driver at all (see kernel/hardened-appliance.config + the README) and cannot
# be made to work by this package. WiFi stays OFF by default regardless
# (hardened posture; harden_radios() in the builder). Ethernet + the tailnet
# are this appliance's ONLY reliable network path.
net-wireless/wpa_supplicant

# ── System ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
app-admin/sudo
sys-process/cronie
sys-apps/haveged
app-editors/nano
app-misc/screen
app-misc/jq

# ── Hardened / security (SELinux LSM) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Same posture as the cluster images: SELinux is the LSM. The policy packages'
# pkg_postinst runs the TARGET `semodule`, which can't execute under an aarch64
# cross-emerge — so the base policy is LOADED AT FIRST BOOT (native) by
# keys-provision (shared engine). See docs/SECURITY.md.
sec-policy/selinux-base
sec-policy/selinux-base-policy
sys-apps/policycoreutils
sys-apps/semodule-utils
sys-apps/checkpolicy
sys-libs/libselinux
sys-libs/libseccomp
sys-process/audit

# NOTE: sys-fs/cryptsetup is NOT listed here — it is appended by the builder
# ONLY when --encrypt-root is set (mirrors specs-frite/specs-orangepi5's
# equivalent comment); install-orangepi-zero2.sh is what actually runs
# luksFormat/open/close on the target hardware at install time.

# ── KEYS USB provisioning + attached storage ────────────────────────────────
# Same first-boot provisioning engine as every other client image: jq parses the
# manifests, dosfstools/util-linux handle the FAT32 KEYS partition + blkid.
net-fs/nfs-utils
net-fs/cifs-utils

# NOTE: headscale + tailscale are NOT emerged here. They are installed as
# upstream static arm64 binaries by build-orangepi-zero2-stage4.sh (the "mesh"
# phase), identical to every other client image. See --skip-mesh / --skip-tailscale.
